               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female, admitted on 09/01/2012 due to acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced exercise tolerance. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed, confirming respiratory compromise consistent with COPD exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia. Lung function assessment supported the diagnosis. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy with good clinical response. She was discharged on 10/01/2012 in a stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure follow-up spirometry. Should symptoms worsen, early reassessment is advised. Kind regards, Dr. [Treating Physician], Department of Internal Medicine.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
